"open":{"price":"The Antalya / Muğla coast row keeps 'est. mid-tier' TRY/m² and 'est. $1,200–$2,000', but the same TCMB Q4 2025 release (Bigpara, 19 Jan 2026) gives Antalya 50,379 and Muğla 76,698 TRY/m². At 46.7 TRY/USD that is about $1,079 and $1,642, and Antalya falls below the est. band. An est. still hides a published figure.","rental":"The penalty table still has 'Listing on platform without permit | 100,000 per property', but Law 7464 mad. 4(1)(d) fines whoever acts as intermediary 'her bir sözleşme için yüz bin' (per contract, not per property), and (e) covers platforms that keep content up 24 h after a warning. Condition 3 (Turkish citizen or legal entity as permit holder) has no source, and the law puts the permit duty on the kiraya veren. Confirmed line 1 is also rejected.","work":"Two worklist lines are not supported by their pages: 'Gerçek usul: full ledger' (the tariff page gives only the brackets; gerçek usul includes işletme-defteri keepers, so 'full ledger' is loose) and the A.Ş. line's 'same kurumlar vergisi' (the Ticaret Bakanlığı page covers only capital). Confirmed lines 9 and 10 are rejected.","risks":"The EKB rows rest on BEP Yönetmeliği mad. 25(15). A secondary report (trtapukadastro.com) cites Danıştay 13. Daire E. 2020/981 K. 2021/1855, which holds that requiring the certificate at tapu transactions goes beyond Law 5627, and ÇŞB Adana's EKB FAQ calls tapu checks only 'planned'. Check the decision and its effect on the 'required at sale' row before closing.","tax":"Condition 2 of the KDV 13/i list ('Property is first sale (ilk teslim) — direct from developer or from Turkish citizen who acquired ≥3 years earlier') contradicts KDV Kanunu md 13/i (mevzuat 1.5.3065), which exempts only the first delivery ('ilk tesliminde') of buildings built as konut or iş yeri; there is no resale route from a citizen after three years. Also the note under the Emlak Vergisi table cites only mad. 8, but the arsa and arazi rows rest on mad. 18."}}
